# Compiled binaries
#
# These are anchored with a leading slash so they match only the build output
# in this directory. Unanchored, "main" and "api" also matched any directory of
# that name at any depth — which silently excluded cmd/api/ (the HTTP API
# entrypoint) from version control entirely.
/bin/
/main
/api

# `go build ./cmd/<name>` drops a binary named after the package into this
# directory, so every command under cmd/ needs its own entry. Build into bin/
# instead (see AGENTS.md) to avoid adding one each time a command is added.
/ingest
/seed_quran
/validate_retrieval

# Test binaries and coverage
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt

# Air (live reload) temp output
/tmp/

# Local env files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
*.log
